    "title": "Burleson's New LDS Temple Opens Doors to Public for First Time in 42 Years - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Isabella Rodriguez ,\n7 hours ago The public will get its first look inside a new Latter-day Saint temple in the Dallas-Fort Worth area in 42 years when the Fort Worth Texas Temple opens for free tours running November 5 through November 21, excluding Sundays. The single-story temple sits at 1851 Greenridge Drive in Burleson, and once it is dedicated in January, only members of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints in good standing will be allowed inside. Read full article\n2",
